  "context_pill": "Marginal Relief for Domestic Companies",
  "example_summary": "Calculating the tax liability and marginal relief for X Ltd., a domestic company whose income slightly exceeds the ₹ 1 Crore surcharge threshold.",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Summary Matrix\n\n| Particulars | Domestic Company (< ₹ 400 Crore Turnover) | Domestic Company (> ₹ 400 Crore Turnover) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Tax Rate** | 25% | 30% |\n| **Surcharge @ Total Income > ₹ 1 Crore to ₹ 10 Crore** | 7% | 7% |\n| **Surcharge @ Total Income > ₹ 10 Crore** | 12% | 12% |\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Marginal Relief Rule:\n> Tax liability including surcharge on total income exceeding ₹ 1 Crore or ₹ 10 Crore shall not exceed the tax payable on total income at the respective threshold plus the amount of income exceeding that threshold.\n\n\n- **Incremental Tax Cap:** Excess tax payable due to higher surcharge cannot be greater than the actual incremental income earned above the threshold limit.\n\n\n- **Non-applicability:** Provisions of Section 115BAA or Section 115BAB offer concessional tax rates with different surcharge dynamics.",
